us_prri: the county roll-up puts Christian at 70.1% against PRRI's published 66%, outside the 2.5 point tolerance. Most likely the categories are not being collapsed into the right nodes -- check the per-node roll-up logged above. Note the published anchors are the article's 2023 figures while the table is a later vintage, so a miss of a point or so is vintage and a miss of ten is a mapping error.
